🧰 Where is URL Encoding Used?
In Web Requests:

Query parameters: ?id=123&name=John%20Doe

Form submissions using application/x-www-form-urlencoded

URLs embedded in links, JavaScript, redirects

In Exploits and CTF Challenges:

Bypassing filters or web application firewalls (WAFs)

Encoding payloads to evade detection

Smuggling malicious inputs past naive validation mechanisms

🎯 Why URL Encoding Matters in CTFs
🔓 Bypassing Input Filters:

A vulnerable app may block ../ but allow %2e%2e%2f (encoded path traversal).

Encoding tricks can help inject payloads undetected.

🎯 Exploiting Web Vulnerabilities:

Used in XSS, LFI, SQLi, and path traversal.

Encoded payloads avoid breaking the structure of the URL.

🛡️ Evading WAFs:

Many WAFs decode inputs once. Double encoding (%252e) can trick them.

🔁 Canonicalization Attacks:

Servers interpret URLs differently depending on how they're decoded.

Useful for access control bypass or directory traversal.
